      "value": "@{5f2c5ef48a580227505d567c|full_name}\n\nI wrote this in a comment above to another user. It does not matter whether they add “native” or “non-native” support. The end result is the same: bones or blendshapes still need to be animated, and the driving parameters still need to be synchronized over the network. There is no meaningful difference.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
